  "conclusions": [
    "LLVM18 O1/O2 on both targets already provides buffer-only ordinary indexed arrays and inlined address-taken locals with144 private bytes and8 user SGPRs; existing6-slot profile does not admit them.",
    "The smallest next runtime experiment is a separate explicitly selected, identity-pinned8-slot buffer-only fixture path preserving the reserved input slots; it is not implemented by this receipt.",
    "Inspect the entire reachable call graph: nested_private has buffer-only entry stores, but call_middle and call_leaf perform actual generic flat private accesses and retain nested calls.",
    "Volatile-inline O2 retains33 stores/2loads. Runtime mixed global/private pointers require preserved generic semantics; proven-private specialization cannot unconditionally rewrite ambiguous pointers.",
    "A noinline nested case with uses_dynamic_stack=false still requires call/stack/flat behavior. Dynamic-stack metadata alone is insufficient admission.",
    "Clang24 removes private storage from simple ordinary probes using register select chains; this does not qualify scratch. It removes unnecessary flat setup from global-only calls, but retains flat scratch for volatile and nested-private probes.",
    "Restricted volatile address-space inference and proof-based internal callee specialization remain possible compiler work, not a verified solution. Preserve generic fallback, volatile order/accesses and callable ABI."
  ],
  "g3_requirement_boundary": "This evidence strengthens the full-call-graph requirement. It neither narrows G3 acceptance nor claims address-taken locals, general generic private pointers or retained nested calls are supported in production.",
